WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
- What I did this
morning was sign the bill

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:06.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
to finally eliminate their
self-governing status.

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:08.775 align:start size:88% position:13%
We've put the area into
state receivership.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.511 align:start size:84% position:16%
I've appointed
people to manage it.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.848
We now have the ability to
apply Florida law to them.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:17.050
They used to be exempt
from the building code

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.518
and all these other things.

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:19.953
We also have the ability now

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that they'll pay their
fair share of taxes,

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.124
which they didn't have to
do for the last 60 years.

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:27.427
And of course, they're gonna
honor all the municipal debt

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:29.396
that they rung up, $700 million.

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:31.765
And so that is, basically,

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:33.967
treating them like
we treat SeaWorld.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:36.369 align:start size:84% position:16%
They're gonna be
just another company.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:39.005
(upbeat music)

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.078
- All right, people.

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.713 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm not even doing a proper
intro for today's show.

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.248
You know the guy.

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.250
I end basically every one
of my daily shows with him,

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.787 align:start size:97% position:3%
the governor of the Free State
of Florida, Ron DeSantis.

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:55.021
Governor, how are you?

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:55.955
- I'm good.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.190
How you doing?

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.691
- I'm all right.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.227 align:start size:97% position:3%
I saw you at the Freedom
Conference this past weekend

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.729
and I said to you

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:05.265 align:start size:97% position:3%
that I'm not gonna bang you
up too much in this interview.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:07.500
I have a feeling you'll
be okay through this one.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.370
So look, everyone knows
how I feel about Florida.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.805
Things are cooking, right?

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:14.307 align:start position:0%
Are you just feeling great
about how things are going here,

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:16.843 align:start size:84% position:16%
'cause that's really
how everyone's
feeling at the moment?

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.478
- Well, there's energy here.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.246
And you're part of it,

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:23.483
because you were in a
place that really used

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:25.685
to be the the place
where people would go

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.487
for the American
Dream, California.

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.856
And to see people
coming 3,000 miles

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.725 align:start size:81% position:19%
to Florida and
being really happy

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
and feeling the
excitement and the energy,

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:37.764 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's really a unique time
in the history of the state.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.532 align:start size:84% position:16%
But it didn't
happen by accident.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.601
I mean, it really was a result

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:84% position:16%
of us making certain
decisions that,

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.440
yes, we were gonna
be a free state.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.810
Yes, we were not gonna end up
becoming a faustian dystopia.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.613
Yes, we're gonna stand
for the right things

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.881
across the board.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.449
And people have
really responded,

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:59.352
as you know, we're the fastest
growing state in the country.

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've led the nation in
net immigration every year

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.089
since I've been governor.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.558 align:start position:0%
And what's happening in
California, Illinois, New York?

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.627
They're having net outmigration.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.295
They're hemorrhaging people.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:11.798
And yes, that's happened
in New York and Illinois

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.700
for a decent amount of time.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.703 align:start size:88% position:13%
But California was never
a place people left.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:21.508
They had never had
net outmigration

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:24.344
until four years ago, from
the time it was a state.

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:26.012
And so I think it's something

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.947 align:start size:84% position:16%
that people are very
sensitive about,

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.150
the state governments
that they live in.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:33.520
There's a wide chasm
between quality of life

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.289
in a place like Florida
where woke goes to die

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:38.057
and some of these other places

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.393
where they're really
embracing woke ideology

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:44.130
to really devastating impacts
on things like public safety

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.865
where people don't feel safe

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.268
in some of these cities anymore

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:51.104
because so much of it's
governed by ideology

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.139 align:start size:88% position:13%
rather than the best
interests of the public.

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:56.176 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So you just bounced around
some of those blue states

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:58.211
and cities to talk
about law enforcement

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.479
and a couple of other things.

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:00.580
We played a bunch
of clips of you.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.382
Were the local officials there,

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:04.817 align:start size:88% position:13%
maybe even the
Democrats, kind of like,

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:07.787 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Hey, Ron, thank
you for coming here,

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.389
and can somebody
fix this thing?"

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:11.691 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, are they
secretly, on the DL,

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:14.727
rooting for someone like you
to show up and fix things?

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.996
'Cause we just know it's not
happening in these blue cities.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.431
- So it's interesting.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:21.568 align:start size:88% position:13%
And the Chicago one
was the most publicized

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:24.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it was with the
Fraternal Order of Police,

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:25.738
a very powerful organization,

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:28.708
and it had been publicized,
I guess, a week in advance.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.411 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so the left in
Illinois was really working

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:34.247 align:start size:88% position:13%
to gin up protest
against me when I came.

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:35.481
So I'm pulling in,

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.717
and this was like an
American Legion hall,

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:38.918
so they had to cap it.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:41.387
There was capacity
for who could get in.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.690
And I'm looking for
these protestors,

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:46.159 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I'm seeing all these
people outside kind

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:47.460
of hooting and hollering,

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.330
and they all had
signs welcoming me.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.966
There were some protestors,
but there weren't very many.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:55.401 align:start size:88% position:13%
But the rest were really
thankful for that.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.903
And so I think the issue is,

00:03:56.903 --> 00:04:00.039 align:start size:97% position:3%
is some of these politicians
cow-towel to the left,

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:02.875 align:start position:0%
the governor there, some of
these people running for mayor.

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:05.011
But I think you go
underneath that,

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.713
and particularly for
individual voters,

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:09.415
regardless if you're a
Republican or Democrat,

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.951 align:start size:88% position:13%
you know that what
they're doing is wrong.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.987 align:start size:84% position:16%
When they just
abolished cash bail

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:15.221
at the beginning of the year,

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:17.257
New York did that and it failed.

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:19.659
Why would you go down that
road if you're Illinois?

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:21.127
Yet, they're doing it.

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.329
So I think people just
want some sanity imposed.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.498
I think they like the
fact that Florida,

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:27.934
we really are common sense
about a lot of this stuff.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.702
But we very much are proud

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:33.139 align:start size:97% position:3%
of being a place where
police officers wanna work,

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.908
because they know that it's
not just me supporting them

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.410
at the state government.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.811
That's important,

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:39.912 align:start size:97% position:3%
'cause if you have a governor
that's not supportive,

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.414
it's bad for morale.

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:43.283 align:start size:88% position:13%
But you go to the
individual communities,

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:45.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
whether it's where you
are down in South Florida,

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:46.753
whether it's the panhandle,

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:50.056 align:start position:0%
people in the communities
genuinely appreciate the people

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:52.325
that wear the uniform and that
makes a difference for them.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:54.560
- I'm down in south
Florida, below Miami.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.996 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't wanna say exactly,
but I met my local mayor here,

00:04:56.996 --> 00:05:01.401
and he told me we have not
had a home break-in 14 years.

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:02.835
14 years!

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.270
It's just nuts.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.472
All right, we have
limited time here.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:11.210
So on the Disney front
and that whole fiasco

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.446
that seemingly has
just disappeared.

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:14.914
You kind of beat the kingdom.

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:17.016
Do you feel like you can
now kind of wash your hands

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:19.252
of this thing, and Disney
will behave differently,

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:22.822
and that there really will be
some concrete changes here?

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:26.993
- Well, actually, what I did
this morning was sign the bill

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
to finally eliminate their
self-governing status.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:32.865 align:start size:88% position:13%
We've put the area into
state receivership.

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:35.034 align:start size:84% position:16%
I've appointed
people to manage it.

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:38.438
We now have the ability to
apply Florida law to them.

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:41.040
They used to be exempt
from the building code

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:41.974
and all these other things.

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.543
We also have the ability now

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:45.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that they'll pay their
fair share of taxes,

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:47.747
which they didn't have to
do for the last 60 years.

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:49.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
And of course, they're
gonna honor all the debts,

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:52.785
the municipal debt, that
they rung up, $700 million.

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:55.955 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so that is
basically treating them

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:57.323
like we treat SeaWorld.

00:05:57.323 --> 00:05:59.726 align:start size:84% position:16%
They're gonna be
just another company.

00:05:59.726 --> 00:06:03.863
And I wish everybody well in
Florida, but here's the thing.

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:08.434
They decided to take political
positions against our policy,

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:09.702
which they have a right to do.

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:10.670
Don't get me wrong.

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.105
But they did that

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:15.007 align:start size:97% position:3%
while enjoying this special
self-governing status

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.609
that no one else
in Florida enjoyed.

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:18.811
They did it while
enjoying subsidies

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.780 align:start size:81% position:19%
and exemptions and
all that stuff.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:21.814
So it's basically,

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:23.850
they're going after our policy

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:26.986 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we're subsidizing
their activism.

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:28.221
So that was untenable.

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:30.757
So I think we had no
choice but to act.

00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:32.258
And so, now, you
have a situation

00:06:32.258 --> 00:06:34.761
where they had one of the
biggest sweetheart deals

00:06:34.761 --> 00:06:38.765
in modern American history
and that is now up in smoke.

00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:40.133
- So since the title

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:43.202
of the book is "The
Courage to Be Free",

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:46.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've heard you, obviously,
publicly and privately,

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:47.573 align:start size:84% position:16%
talk about fighting
with the media.

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:50.009 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I get a sense that
you really like it.

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:52.478
You kind of like when
they go after you.

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:54.380 align:start size:97% position:3%
It doesn't even matter
which side it's coming from.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:57.116
Is that something that you
kind of learned on the job

00:06:57.116 --> 00:07:01.287 align:start position:0%
or did you always have that
kind of innate courage yourself?

00:07:01.287 --> 00:07:05.658
- Well, I think in terms of
just the courage to stand

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:08.828 align:start size:97% position:3%
for what's right and for
freedom, in this day and age,

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:11.697
as you know, so many of
the elite institutions

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:14.901 align:start size:97% position:3%
in our society, including
the media, but also big tech,

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:19.672
also the major corporations,
universities, the bureaucracy,

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:24.076
they are pursuing a more
woke left-of-center agenda.

00:07:24.076 --> 00:07:27.280 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so if you're somebody
that's an impediment to that,

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.015
if I'm standing here
in Florida, and saying,

00:07:29.015 --> 00:07:30.049
"No, no, not on my watch.

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:31.851
This is where woke goes to die."

00:07:31.851 --> 00:07:34.053
Well, they're not
gonna like that,

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:35.154
and they're gonna come at you

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:36.889
and they're gonna shoot at you,

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:39.325
and you've gotta be
willing to take that

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:41.027 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you've gotta be
willing to fight back.

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:43.796
But if you're somebody that
thinks, in this day and age,

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:46.799 align:start size:97% position:3%
standing for the right
things is gonna be cost-free,

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:49.235
then you're in the
wrong line of work.

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:51.938 align:start size:81% position:19%
And so it's not
that you enjoy it,

00:07:51.938 --> 00:07:53.739
but I view it as
positive feedback,

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:58.711
when I have all these Democrat
governors just attacking me,

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:02.448
unilaterally, I have the
New York media obsessed

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:03.716
with attacking me.

00:08:03.716 --> 00:08:05.952
Well, they wouldn't
be doing that, Dave,

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:08.654
if I wasn't effective and if
I wasn't making a difference.

00:08:08.654 --> 00:08:10.156
And so that tells me we're

00:08:10.156 --> 00:08:12.692
on the right track and
we've gotta keep going.

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:15.061
But it's not just a guy like
me who's governing a big state.

00:08:15.061 --> 00:08:16.529
Yeah, I'm a target.

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:19.832
You have parents that have
gone to school board meetings

00:08:19.832 --> 00:08:21.701 align:start size:88% position:13%
to raise concerns about
some of the things

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:23.402
that are going on in the schools

00:08:23.402 --> 00:08:25.037
and they get smeared by media.

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:28.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hell, Merrick Garland
wanted to mobilize the FBI

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:31.477
to go after some of the parents.

00:08:31.477 --> 00:08:32.745
Whatever level you're at,

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:36.115
just know that there
will be some pushback.

00:08:36.115 --> 00:08:40.653 align:start position:0%
But ultimately, if we wanna
maintain Florida as a free state

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:43.089
and if we wanna have a
revival across America,

00:08:43.089 --> 00:08:46.259
where our true principles are
honored, that makes us unique,

00:08:46.259 --> 00:08:48.561
you're gonna have to
fight these fights

00:08:48.561 --> 00:08:51.731
and you are gonna have
to pay a certain price

00:08:51.731 --> 00:08:53.799 align:start size:84% position:16%
in terms of what
people say about you

00:08:53.799 --> 00:08:56.435
and the opposition
that you generate.

00:08:56.435 --> 00:08:58.738 align:start position:0%
- Right, and we show the
pictures pretty much every day.

00:08:58.738 --> 00:09:00.673
But the same media guys
who are going after you,

00:09:00.673 --> 00:09:02.108 align:start size:88% position:13%
they end up vacationing
in Miami Beach

00:09:02.108 --> 00:09:03.876 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the panhandle
and everywhere else.

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:07.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
All right, I will ask you,
actually, one tough one

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.081
so this isn't all
softball stuff.

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:12.351 align:start position:0%
In terms of the amount of
people that are coming here now,

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:14.654
and last I heard it was
about 1,200 people a day,

00:09:14.654 --> 00:09:17.690
the one thing that seems to be
tough in Florida right now is

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:18.925
that housing prices are,

00:09:18.925 --> 00:09:21.060
because of the amount
of people coming in,

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.395
housing prices are rising.

00:09:22.395 --> 00:09:23.963 align:start size:84% position:16%
They seem to be rising
across the country

00:09:23.963 --> 00:09:25.398 align:start size:84% position:16%
even in places
people are fleeing.

00:09:25.398 --> 00:09:27.700 align:start size:81% position:19%
But what can be
done on that front

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:29.735 align:start size:84% position:16%
so that the OG
Floridians don't feel

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:31.470
like they're getting pushed out

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:34.173 align:start position:0%
and all the new people feel
like they can get a fair price?

00:09:34.173 --> 00:09:36.142
- Yeah, no, it's
a great question.

00:09:36.142 --> 00:09:39.245 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, on the one hand, we're
a victim of our own success

00:09:39.245 --> 00:09:41.280 align:start size:88% position:13%
on that because the
demand is high to live,

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.015
particularly where you're at.

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:44.884
Well, one thing we are gonna do,

00:09:44.884 --> 00:09:47.954
we're gonna accelerate a lot
of our infrastructure projects.

00:09:47.954 --> 00:09:50.389
So I have a bunch of
projects in the hopper

00:09:50.389 --> 00:09:52.658 align:start size:84% position:16%
that are important for
alleviating traffic,
all this stuff,

00:09:52.658 --> 00:09:53.960
all across the state.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.362
We're putting an
extra $7 billion in

00:09:56.362 --> 00:09:59.932
so that I can get those done
13 years ahead of schedule.

00:09:59.932 --> 00:10:01.567
'Cause some of these
are on a 20-year plan.

00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:02.735
We don't have 20 years.

00:10:02.735 --> 00:10:04.403
Too many people are coming.

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:06.739
So having that infrastructure
in place I think is important.

00:10:06.739 --> 00:10:09.742
That can also make
it easier to continue

00:10:09.742 --> 00:10:11.277
to build new housing.

00:10:11.277 --> 00:10:14.180 align:start size:84% position:16%
We do have it going
up all over the state,

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:15.414
like never before,

00:10:15.414 --> 00:10:18.150 align:start size:84% position:16%
but it still hasn't
kept pace with demand.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:20.519
So the legislature
is gonna do a bill

00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:24.924
to try to address some of
the needs in certain areas.

00:10:24.924 --> 00:10:27.393
And it's not just
about the people

00:10:27.393 --> 00:10:30.830
that can afford the big houses
in the suburbs that are nice.

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:33.199 align:start size:97% position:3%
We have a lot of people
who are very working class,

00:10:33.199 --> 00:10:36.202 align:start size:97% position:3%
working jobs, maybe they're
waitress or something,

00:10:36.202 --> 00:10:38.237
and it's hard to
find an apartment

00:10:38.237 --> 00:10:40.373
in certain parts of the state.

00:10:40.373 --> 00:10:42.475 align:start size:97% position:3%
So we wanna see more of
that type of housing be able

00:10:42.475 --> 00:10:43.743
to be built.

00:10:43.743 --> 00:10:45.511 align:start size:88% position:13%
So there's gonna be a
big package that's done,

00:10:45.511 --> 00:10:47.279
and I think it'll help.

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:49.215
But at the end of the day,

00:10:49.215 --> 00:10:51.951
we've always been a
state that's grown.

00:10:51.951 --> 00:10:53.419
We are building,

00:10:53.419 --> 00:10:55.588 align:start size:84% position:16%
but man, the growth
is outstripping

00:10:55.588 --> 00:10:58.057
how fast these guys
can build the homes.

00:10:58.057 --> 00:11:00.026 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now, of course, the inflation
has been a huge problem,

00:11:00.026 --> 00:11:02.762
'cause construction costs
have gone through the roof.

00:11:02.762 --> 00:11:06.599 align:start size:97% position:3%
So what used to be a home
in some excerpt for 250,000,

00:11:06.599 --> 00:11:10.302 align:start position:0%
now that costs more so that
they gotta charge over 300,000,

00:11:10.302 --> 00:11:11.771
put aside the demand,

00:11:11.771 --> 00:11:14.607
and of course, the demand
drives it even higher.

00:11:14.607 --> 00:11:15.841
- How much do you feel

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:17.977
like you're fighting
the federal government

00:11:17.977 --> 00:11:19.011
on a daily basis?

00:11:19.011 --> 00:11:20.479
I mean, obviously,

00:11:20.479 --> 00:11:23.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
they cut FEMA kind of
early after Hurricane Ian.

00:11:23.015 --> 00:11:26.152 align:start size:84% position:16%
The general stuff
with inflation, as
you just referenced,

00:11:26.152 --> 00:11:29.055 align:start size:97% position:3%
the DIE stuff that we're
doing things here in Florida

00:11:29.055 --> 00:11:30.623
that they're pushing federally.

00:11:30.623 --> 00:11:32.491
I mean, do you really feel
like you're just constantly

00:11:32.491 --> 00:11:35.728
at odds with them, and does
it even matter, I guess?

00:11:35.728 --> 00:11:36.962
- Yeah, I mean, look,

00:11:36.962 --> 00:11:39.031
I think that we are
protecting Floridians

00:11:39.031 --> 00:11:41.934
with all that we've got
against the excesses

00:11:41.934 --> 00:11:43.569
of the Biden administration.

00:11:43.569 --> 00:11:45.071
I mean, for example,

00:11:45.071 --> 00:11:48.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
they did the MRNA vax
mandate for the hospitals.

00:11:48.307 --> 00:11:50.710
And that was done under CMS.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had all these nurses,
they didn't wanna take it.

00:11:53.345 --> 00:11:55.314
A lot of them had
already had COVID.

00:11:55.314 --> 00:11:57.283
Many of them had concerns.

00:11:57.283 --> 00:11:59.785 align:start position:0%
And so I didn't think they
should lose their job over that.

00:11:59.785 --> 00:12:01.587
But they were gonna
impose this mandate.

00:12:01.587 --> 00:12:03.789
However, they required the State

00:12:03.789 --> 00:12:07.560 align:start size:97% position:3%
of Florida's hospital agency
to survey the hospitals

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:10.429 align:start size:84% position:16%
to ensure that the
vaxes were being done.

00:12:10.429 --> 00:12:11.664
We rejected that.

00:12:11.664 --> 00:12:14.500
We decided that we are
not gonna help this.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.969 align:start position:0%
And so they didn't have the
ability to get the information.

00:12:16.969 --> 00:12:19.338
They find us, which is fine.

00:12:19.338 --> 00:12:20.740
Find me, I don't care.

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:22.975
We saved tens of
thousands of jobs

00:12:22.975 --> 00:12:24.610
across the State of Florida.

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:28.180
So anytime we can step in and
protect people against this,

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:30.616 align:start size:81% position:19%
we do and we'll
continue to do it.

00:12:30.616 --> 00:12:32.017
But here just shows
you what's going on

00:12:32.017 --> 00:12:33.519
in the administration.

00:12:33.519 --> 00:12:37.323
You know that the FDA forced
through emergency approval

00:12:37.323 --> 00:12:40.192 align:start size:84% position:16%
for MNRA vax for
six-month old babies.

00:12:40.192 --> 00:12:41.427
They didn't have data.

00:12:41.427 --> 00:12:43.262
They didn't show
it was a benefit,

00:12:43.262 --> 00:12:44.797
but they rammed it through.

00:12:44.797 --> 00:12:48.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
Meanwhile, I've had an
application under 2003 law

00:12:48.701 --> 00:12:51.270 align:start size:88% position:13%
that I did during
Trump's administration.

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:54.673
It's been sitting with Biden
for over two years at the FDA

00:12:54.673 --> 00:12:57.810
where my state agencies can
purchase drugs from Canada.

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:00.012
The same drugs that
we already buy here.

00:13:00.012 --> 00:13:01.280
They're just cheaper.

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:02.581
There's a provision
of law as we do it.

00:13:02.581 --> 00:13:06.152
FDA says, "Well, we're
not sure it's safe."

00:13:06.152 --> 00:13:08.788 align:start size:84% position:16%
So they'll stick
six-month old babies

00:13:08.788 --> 00:13:11.724
with an MNRA shot on
an emergency basis,

00:13:11.724 --> 00:13:14.426
but they won't let
me buy these drugs.

00:13:14.426 --> 00:13:15.961
No, of course,

00:13:15.961 --> 00:13:17.630
what they're doing is they're
basically running interference

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:18.864
for big pharma,

00:13:18.864 --> 00:13:21.333 align:start size:88% position:13%
and that's typical of
what Biden's been doing.

00:13:21.333 --> 00:13:22.434
So it's frustrating.

00:13:22.434 --> 00:13:24.069
But I think that we've done...

00:13:24.069 --> 00:13:25.304
And oh, by the way,

00:13:25.304 --> 00:13:27.740
and maybe you can break
this when it happens,

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:31.944
we have a case in front of the
Northern District of Florida

00:13:31.944 --> 00:13:33.445
in the panhandle

00:13:33.445 --> 00:13:36.749
on Biden's catch-and-release
immigration amnesty policies.

00:13:36.749 --> 00:13:38.350
We're gonna win that case.

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:40.219 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's been submitted
to the court.

00:13:40.219 --> 00:13:42.054 align:start size:84% position:16%
We're just waiting
for the judge to rule.

00:13:42.054 --> 00:13:45.191 align:start size:97% position:3%
We think it's gonna be
probably sometime in March,

00:13:45.191 --> 00:13:48.828
and I think it's gonna
say his catch-and-release

00:13:48.828 --> 00:13:50.396
is unconstitutional.

00:13:50.396 --> 00:13:52.898 align:start size:84% position:16%
If that's (indistinct)
nationwide,

00:13:52.898 --> 00:13:54.400
they're gonna have

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:55.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
to reevaluate their entire
open border policies.

00:13:55.801 --> 00:13:58.404 align:start size:84% position:16%
So we're fighting
back on a daily basis.

00:13:58.404 --> 00:14:01.473 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, governor,
you have blueprinted
this thing quite well

00:14:01.473 --> 00:14:03.576
which is why me and
my family moved here

00:14:03.576 --> 00:14:05.311 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I'm proud to be
in the fight with you.

00:14:05.311 --> 00:14:06.712
And now, I got one more for you.

00:14:06.712 --> 00:14:08.147
I know you're on a massive blitz

00:14:08.147 --> 00:14:09.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you gotta get to
number one New York Times,

00:14:09.648 --> 00:14:11.317 align:start size:84% position:16%
although the ultimate
credit would be

00:14:11.317 --> 00:14:12.852
if they don't put you on at all

00:14:12.852 --> 00:14:14.987
because then you can really
stick it to them, of course.

00:14:14.987 --> 00:14:16.222
But is there any other sort

00:14:16.222 --> 00:14:17.790
of announcement you
might wanna make,

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.525
or anything else you
might wanna talk about,

00:14:19.525 --> 00:14:22.027
as long as we're
just chatting here,

00:14:22.027 --> 00:14:23.896 align:start size:88% position:13%
anything else you wanna
say about anything?

00:14:23.896 --> 00:14:25.397
Or, we could just end this now.

00:14:25.397 --> 00:14:26.432
You tell me.

00:14:26.432 --> 00:14:28.234
- Wouldn't you like to know?

00:14:28.234 --> 00:14:30.035
I mean, that'd be
a good one for you.

00:14:30.035 --> 00:14:33.272 align:start size:84% position:16%
But no, listen, I
appreciate your story,

00:14:33.272 --> 00:14:35.174
and I'm really appreciative

00:14:35.174 --> 00:14:37.276
that you really like
the State of Florida.

00:14:37.276 --> 00:14:38.777
'Cause I have similar stories

00:14:38.777 --> 00:14:41.080 align:start size:97% position:3%
and it makes us feel like
we're doing the right thing.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:43.382
So if people go to
desantisbook.com,

00:14:43.382 --> 00:14:47.987 align:start size:84% position:16%
they can see some
of the policies that
kind of led to that.

00:14:47.987 --> 00:14:49.421 align:start size:84% position:16%
But when people stop
you on the street

00:14:49.421 --> 00:14:53.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
and thank you for creating
a great environment,

00:14:53.392 --> 00:14:55.661
that's why you get
into this business,

00:14:55.661 --> 00:14:57.563 align:start size:84% position:16%
that's why you deal
with all the BS

00:14:57.563 --> 00:14:59.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you gotta deal
with, because ultimately,

00:14:59.999 --> 00:15:01.300
you're helping make
people's lives better

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:02.935
and we've been able
to do that here.

00:15:02.935 --> 00:15:04.203
- Gov, I'll just tell
you one last thing.

00:15:04.203 --> 00:15:05.671
So when I moved here

00:15:05.671 --> 00:15:06.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm walking my dog
and everybody's coming up,

00:15:06.972 --> 00:15:08.807 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Oh, you're the new
guys living over there."

00:15:08.807 --> 00:15:09.742 align:start size:84% position:16%
And they say, "Where
are you from?"

00:15:09.742 --> 00:15:11.176
And I'd go, "Cali, Los Angeles",

00:15:11.176 --> 00:15:12.678
and they start freaking out.

00:15:12.678 --> 00:15:14.780
So I realize what I should do
is I have to keep a picture

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:16.482 align:start size:84% position:16%
of me and you
together on my phone.

00:15:16.482 --> 00:15:19.752
So when they say it, I go,
"No, no, no, I know this guy.

00:15:19.752 --> 00:15:21.320
And then everybody's
like, "We're good."

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:22.988 align:start size:84% position:16%
Governor, the book's
gonna crush it.

00:15:22.988 --> 00:15:24.189
I appreciate you.

00:15:24.189 --> 00:15:25.724
You helped change my
life by getting me here

00:15:25.724 --> 00:15:27.960 align:start size:84% position:16%
and my whole team
and two companies now

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:29.495
with Rumble and Locals.

00:15:29.495 --> 00:15:32.298
So thank you and hope to see
you and the first lady soon.

00:15:32.298 --> 00:15:33.899
- Okay, take care.

00:15:33.899 --> 00:15:35.100
Thanks.

